wiz3d (0.3.1+stereo3d4) testing; urgency=medium

  * wiz3d-run uses the shared stereo_declare module (python3-stereo-declare
    1.2.0, from libstereo-declare) instead of carrying its own copy of the
    declaration; what it does and prints is unchanged.
  * New: wiz3d-launch, which puts wiz3D in a Wine prefix beside DXVK, runs
    the game through wiz3d-run and takes wiz3D out again (WIZ3D_LOG_DIR keeps
    wiz3D's logs out of the prefix and the game folder).
  * The fork is now github.com/Sparky-OS/wiz3D (Vcs fields).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0300

wiz3d (0.3.1+stereo3d3) testing; urgency=medium

  * The proxy and the wrapper take the real Direct3D 9 from d3d9_real.dll
    when it sits beside the proxy, so a Wine prefix manager can install
    wiz3D in the prefix as it installs DXVK.
  * WIZ3D_LOG_DIR moves wiz3D's log files and Statistic.xml out of the game
    folder and the prefix.
  * Built from the fork rebased on effcol/wiz3D main (Linux build merged
    upstream in #33).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0300

wiz3d (0.3.1+stereo3d1) testing; urgency=medium

  * Packaging of the Sparky Stereo OS fork (danielcamposramos/wiz3D, branch
    partner/wiz3d-proton, upstream effcol/wiz3D v0.3.1): Direct3D 9 chain
    built with clang-cl and xwin, full side by side as the only output
    plug-in, wiz3d-run launcher declaring through libstereo-declare.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0300
